From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: an MLO client is somewhere too
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

sta.agent_almac was never updated for an MLO client, on any path.

A legacy client is carried in the Associated Clients TLV and that is where its
node is learned. An MLO client is not: agent_gen_assoc_client_tlv() skips
affiliated stations by design, because they belong in the Associated STA MLD
Config TLV instead - and the MLD address does not appear in the first TLV at
all. So the row for an MLO client stays wherever it last was, forever, and
nothing corrects it.

Measured 2026-09-06 on the lab mesh:

    hardware   ba:a9:1b:53:17:82 on the corridor node, three legs
               (2.4 / 5 / 6 GHz), all affiliated, live
    sta        attached to the controller, 1862 s old
    sta_mld    right AP-MLD, 2184 s old

Every reader that asks which node a client is on - the topology picture, the
per-node client count, steering, assoc_control - was answered wrongly for
exactly the client type this project exists for.

The Associated STA MLD Config TLV is that client's own statement of where it
is. It names the client and the AP-MLD, and the AP-MLD is matched against the
reporting node's own list before this runs, so nothing is inferred.

Two nodes do report the same client, and num_aff settles it. A node the client
has left keeps the STA-MLD in its list for a while and reports it with ZERO
affiliated stations - measured the same day, the corridor node reporting ba:a9
with 0 legs while the bedroom node reported 2 (6 GHz at -52 dBm and 5 GHz) and
the corridor node's wifi layer had nothing at all. An MLD with no affiliated
station is not attached anywhere, so such a report is not read as a claim.
That is not a tie-breaker bolted on; it is what the field means. Without it the
two reports alternate and the client's node flips with each - measured twice
within one second.

Only a client already in the model is moved. Creating one from this path would
add a second way for stations to enter the model, and 99999996 is what that
costs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SmdHaYcnhtvUuXYfnXZobZ

--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -5112,6 +5112,67 @@
 		if (!match)
 			continue;
 
+		/* Say where this client is, in the table everything else reads.
+		 *
+		 * An MLO client never appears in the Associated Clients TLV:
+		 * agent_gen_assoc_client_tlv() skips affiliated stations by
+		 * design - they belong here instead - and the MLD address is
+		 * not in that TLV at all. So the path that keeps a legacy
+		 * client's node current simply does not exist for an MLO one,
+		 * and its row stays wherever it last was.
+		 *
+		 * Measured 2026-09-06: ba:a9:1b:53:17:82 live on one node with
+		 * three legs and recorded in sta as attached to another, 1862 s
+		 * old. Every reader that asks which node a client is on - the
+		 * picture, the client count, steering, assoc_control - was
+		 * answered wrongly for the one client type this project exists
+		 * for.
+		 *
+		 * num_aff is what settles it when two nodes report the same
+		 * client, and they do: a node the client has left keeps the
+		 * STA-MLD in its list for a while and reports it with ZERO
+		 * affiliated stations. Measured the same day, minutes apart -
+		 * the corridor node reported ba:a9 with 0 legs while the
+		 * bedroom node reported it with 2 (6 GHz at -52 dBm and 5 GHz),
+		 * and the wifi layer on the corridor node had nothing at all.
+		 *
+		 * An MLD with no affiliated station is not attached anywhere.
+		 * Such a report says nothing about where the client is, so it
+		 * is not read as a claim. This is not a tie-breaker bolted on;
+		 * it is what the field means.
+		 *
+		 * Without it the two reports alternate and the client's node
+		 * flips with each one - measured, twice within a single second.
+		 *
+		 * Only a client already known is moved. Creating one from this
+		 * path would add a second way for stations to enter the model,
+		 * and 99999996 is what that costs.
+		 */
+		if (num_aff > 0) {
+			struct sta *cs;
+
+			cs = cntlr_find_sta(c->sta_table, (uint8_t *)sta_mac);
+			if (cs) {
+				if (memcmp(cs->agent_almacaddr, n->almacaddr, 6)) {
+					struct node *old_n;
+
+					cntlr_info(LOG_STA, "%s: MLD client " MACFMT
+						   " is on node " MACFMT " with %u link(s)"
+						   " (was " MACFMT ")\n",
+						   __func__, MAC2STR(cs->macaddr),
+						   MAC2STR(n->almacaddr), num_aff,
+						   MAC2STR(cs->agent_almacaddr));
+
+					old_n = cntlr_find_node(c, cs->agent_almacaddr);
+					if (old_n)
+						node_del_sta(old_n, cs);
+
+					node_add_sta(n, cs);
+				}
+				cs->state = STA_CONNECTED;
+			}
+		}
+
 		list_for_each_entry(e, &match->stamldlist, list) {
 			if (!memcmp(e->mld_macaddr, sta_mac, 6)) {
 				sm = e;
